{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hidden-hemp-condor","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit review of change 1874 observed that docs/event-schema.md lists six canonical LINK relations but omits the already-supported caused_by relation. The packaged CLI overview lists caused_by, and closed task isogonal-wedded-catfish is the design/implementation authority adding it as the seventh directional, non-blocking, non-cycle-inducing relation.\n\n## Investigation and repair plan\n\n- Reproduce the maintained-documentation mismatch against current origin/main and cite the authoritative implementation/design surfaces.\n- Under rebar-debug, prove whether the omission is a stale inventory rather than a runtime defect.\n- Add a held-out documentation contract that exercises the maintained event-schema surface and preserves relation semantics.\n- Repair only the proven documentation omission, run exact-defect mutation, focused documentation gates, lint, and typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] docs/event-schema.md includes caused_by in the canonical LINK relation inventory.\n- [ ] The documentation states caused_by is directional, non-blocking, and non-cycle-inducing consistently with the implemented contract.\n- [ ] A behavior-level documentation contract is RED before repair, GREEN after repair, and returns RED under the exact omission mutation.\n- [ ] Documentation gates, lint, and typecheck pass.","id":"6532-9285-1808-40ea","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["docs","links","parity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Document caused_by in the event-schema relation inventory"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787091229521723001,"uuid":"361f2e57-36ac-4007-a3f0-39a42b1c5a67"}